{"schema_version":1,"id":"residual","title":"Residual learners and null controls","generated":"2026-10-30T18:12:57Z","generated_from":"gallery/data/export_ml.py","file":"ml/residual.json","text":{"finding":"On the 239 Addis filters (time-blocked folds) the HIPS/10 − f(X) relation is b = 0.802·f(X) + 2.851, so the residual carries 0.198·f(X) by construction. A learner given only f(X) reaches residual R² 0.064, inside the no-information null (median 0.077, p = 0.67); the spectra learner reaches 0.244, above the null's q95 0.113 (ftir_43). Paired against f(X) + season + volume + lot on the same blocks, the spectra gain ΔRMSE -0.060 µg/m³ [-0.134, +0.020] is not significant (it does beat the null: q95 +0.031); with gravimetric mass in the base it becomes -0.126 [-0.199, -0.032] (ftir_46). No named feature carries the increment (ftir_45). At fixed f(X) and season the residual falls -0.068 µg/m³ per µg/m³ of mass [-0.097, -0.045]: the lead is loading, and the mass term is two to three times larger at the Ethiopian sites than elsewhere."},"sources":[{"table":"model_comparison","rows":6,"notebook":"ftir_43_residual_learner_null_control","read":"executed notebook output","path":"research/ftir_ec_phase3/ftir_43_residual_learner_null_control.ipynb","cell":"results.to_csv(OUT / 'model_comparison.csv'"},{"table":"null_distribution_summary","rows":2,"notebook":"ftir_43_residual_learner_null_control","read":"executed notebook output","path":"research/ftir_ec_phase3/ftir_43_residual_learner_null_control.ipynb","cell":"null_summary.to_csv"},{"table":"null_relation","rows":1,"notebook":"ftir_43_residual_learner_null_control","read":"executed notebook output (printed)","path":"research/ftir_ec_phase3/ftir_43_residual_learner_null_control.ipynb","cell":"load_addis_evaluation()"},{"table":"stepwise_attribution","rows":6,"notebook":"ftir_45_residual_increment_attribution","read":"executed notebook output","path":"research/ftir_ec_phase3/ftir_45_residual_increment_attribution.ipynb","cell